,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[1,2,1,2,1,2,1,2,2,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8]],"output":[[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[2,2,2,2,2,2,2,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8],[8,8,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,3,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8],[2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,8,8,8,8,3,8,8],[8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,8,3,8,8]]}]},"teaching_variant":"canonical","teacher_models":["claude-opus-5-5"],"explanation":"**What the grid is made of.** Each input has three kinds of thing on a background of 8:\n- one green 3 cell sitting on a grid edge (the seed);\n- several straight bars of 2;\n- some 1 cells mixed into one end of each bar.\n\nEvery bar runs from a grid edge into the open field.\n\n**What the output does.**\n- Every 1 becomes 2.\n- From the seed, a green path heads into the grid, straight away from the edge the seed sits on.\n- When the path meets a bar, it stops a little before it. It then runs sideways past the bar's free end, the end that does not touch the edge. Once it is beyond that end, it turns back to its original direction and carries on. It repeats this at every bar and finally runs off the opposite edge.\n\n**How far the path stays from a bar.** The clearance is the number of 1s in that bar plus one. The path stops that many cells before the bar. It then goes that many cells past the bar's free end. Checking this against the demonstrations:\n- **Pair 1:** the bar has 4 ones, so the clearance is 5. The bar is in row 7, and the path stops at row 2. The bar's free end is at x=6, and the path turns down at x=1.\n- **Pair 2:** the first bar has 1 one, so the clearance is 2. The path stops at x=4 and passes below the bar's end at row 6, reaching row 8. The second bar touches the bottom and has 3 ones, so the clearance is 4. The path stops at x=12 and goes up to row 7−4=3.\n- **Pair 3:**\n  - The first bar has 1 one, giving a clearance of 2. The path turns at row 2 and goes right to x=8.\n  - The second bar has 2 ones, giving a clearance of 3. The path turns at row 7 and goes left to x=1.\n  - The third bar has 2 ones, giving a clearance of 3. The path turns at row 13 and goes right to x=8.\n- **Pair 4** follows the same pattern.\n\n**Query inputs.**\n- **Test 1:** the seed is on the right edge, so the path moves left. It passes these bars:\n  - the bar at x=17, which touches the top and has 3 ones (clearance 4);\n  - the bar at x=7, which touches the bottom and has 2 ones (clearance 3);\n  - the bar at x=1, which touches the top and has 1 one (clearance 2).\n- **Test 2:** the seed is on the top edge, so the path moves down. It weaves past four horizontal bars, going around each one on its open side.\n\n**How the program works.** It finds the bars as multicolour connected components of 2 and 1. It walks the path one straight segment at a time and emits a checkpoint after each segment.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    H, W = g.shape\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    sy, sx = [tuple(p) for p in np.argwhere(g == 3)][0]\n    mask = (g != bg) & (g != 3)\n    comps = components(mask)\n    lab = {}\n    for i, c in enumerate(comps):\n        for p in c:\n            lab[p] = i\n    out[g == 1] = 2\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Recolour every 1 inside the bars to 2.\")\n    if sy == 0: d = (1, 0)\n    elif sy == H - 1: d = (-1, 0)\n    elif sx == 0: d = (0, 1)\n    else: d = (0, -1)\n    y, x = sy, sx\n    inside = lambda a, b: 0 <= a < H and 0 <= b < W\n    for _ in range(50):\n        dy, dx = d\n        # scan ahead for first bar cell\n        ty, tx, hit = y + dy, x + dx, None\n        while inside(ty, tx):\n            if (ty, tx) in lab:\n                hit = lab[(ty, tx)]; break\n            ty += dy; tx += dx\n        if hit is None:\n            ty, tx = y + dy, x + dx\n            while inside(ty, tx):\n                out[ty, tx] = 3; ty += dy; tx += dx\n            emit(out.copy(), \"No bar ahead: run the green path straight to the edge.\")\n            break\n        cells = comps[hit]\n        k = sum(1 for p in cells if g[p] == 1) + 1\n        # stop k cells before the bar\n        stop = (ty - dy * k, tx - dx * k)\n        while (y, x) != stop:\n            y += dy; x += dx; out[y, x] = 3\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Approach the bar, stopping {k} cells before it (1s + 1).\")\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = bbox(cells)\n        if dy != 0:  # horizontal bar, sidestep along x\n            if x0 == 0: target, sd = x1 + k, (0, 1)\n            elif x1 == W - 1: target, sd = x0 - k, (0, -1)\n            else:\n                target, sd = (x1 + k, (0, 1)) if W - 1 - x1 > x0 else (x0 - k, (0, -1))\n            target = max(0, min(W - 1, target))\n            while x != target:\n                x += sd[1]; out[y, x] = 3\n        else:\n            if y0 == 0: target, sd = y1 + k, (1, 0)\n            elif y1 == H - 1: target, sd = y0 - k, (-1, 0)\n            else:\n                target, sd = (y1 + k, (1, 0)) if H - 1 - y1 > y0 else (y0 - k, (-1, 0))\n            target = max(0, min(H - 1, target))\n            while y != target:\n                y += sd[0]; out[y, x] = 3\n        emit(out.copy(), f\"Sidestep around the bar's free end, {k} cells beyond it.\")\n    emit(out.copy(), \"Final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"objects":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How the program works.** It finds the bars as multicolour connected components of 2 and 1."}],"recolour":[{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Recolour every 1 inside the bars to 2."}],"paths":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- From the seed, a green path heads into the grid, straight away from the edge the seed sits on."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"- When the path meets a bar, it stops a little before it."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How far the path stays from a bar.** The clearance is the number of 1s in that bar plus one."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"**How far the path stays from a bar.** The clearance is the number of 1s in that bar plus one."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"a33e42fd6a11f6d1448b54abd8485c5fd7e98cb6c46be1667d17bce73e6dfaaa","task_sha256":"b7b796dbcff9c540fa00009a83108c3b7d67e47b2b364a985d9c5f1d871f8d93","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synthetic generalization not established."}
